messy-ui — licensing summary
============================

This repository is covered by two licences. Which one applies depends on which
part of the tree the code lives in.

1. Component registry and site — MIT
------------------------------------

Everything in this repository EXCEPT the PDF toolkit (see section 2) is
released under the MIT licence reproduced below. That includes `registry/`,
which is what `npx shadcn add` copies into your project, and the rest of the
site.

2. PDF toolkit — separate licence
---------------------------------

These paths are NOT covered by the MIT licence:

    src/lib/pdf/
    src/components/pdf/
    src/app/pdf/
    scripts/copy-static-assets.mjs
    scripts/smoke/pdf-smoke.mjs

They are source-available under the terms in `LICENSE-PDF`. In short: read it,
learn from it, run it yourself, and use the hosted version at
https://messyui.dev/pdf free of charge forever — but shipping it inside a
product needs a commercial licence.

Third-party code
----------------

`src/lib/pdf/sign/placeholder.ts` is derived from @signpdf
(https://github.com/vbuch/node-signpdf), MIT licensed, and carries its
attribution in the file header. Runtime dependencies keep their own licences.


